# Source location: https://github.com/MelkhiorVintageComputing/RD68041
#
# The screens `make quadra-m68040` accepts as the end of the boot, one a line:
#   <machine> <sha256 of the screen's RGB pixels, first 16 hex digits> <what it shows>
# MAME is deterministic: the same build, ROMs and options give the same
# screen. The PNGs themselves are never committed (Apple firmware output).
# (Until M14 the hash was of the PNG file, which carries the machine's name:
# make quadra compares the core's machines' screens with these.)
# With the zero-filled stand-in for the ADB modem's PIC firmware (no
# 342s0440-b.bin supplied), the ROM stops in ADB initialisation on the grey
# desktop pattern (doc/oracles.md, "MAME's Quadra").
macqd650 918a7cb9026e618c grey desktop, ADB initialisation waiting (stand-in ADB firmware)
macct650 918a7cb9026e618c grey desktop, ADB initialisation waiting (stand-in ADB firmware)
